  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "labelRecursivePatterns",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/SmilesParse/SmilesParse.cpp",
    "description": "`labelRecursivePatterns()` unconditionally pops from its local `state` stack when it sees `')'` (`state.back(); state.pop_back();`) without ensuring there is a matching prior push. With malformed SMARTS containing excess closing parentheses, the initial BASE element can be popped and subsequent `)` operations execute on an empty `std::list`, corrupting list internals and later causing an invalid free (ASan bad-free in list::pop_back destructor path). Crash is observed during destruction/pop_back, but root cause is missing balance/underflow validation in this function.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzed molfile reaches `ParseMarvinSmartsLine()` (MRV SMA property), which passes attacker-controlled SMARTS text to `SmartsToMol()`, which always calls `labelRecursivePatterns()`. Input SMARTS must include unmatched/extra `)` (e.g., many closing parens) so `state` underflows in `labelRecursivePatterns`. This malformed recursive-pattern relabeling state then triggers memory corruption and bad-free."
  },
